  "identityStatus": "Complete source model of the mapped above-ground Shibuya JR/Ginza passenger-station exterior: both whole mapped JR island platforms and longitudinal canopy families, the Hachiko-side entrance frontage, central raised concourse, new south hall and south platform covers, the full elevated Ginza terminal with its characteristic white M-section roof/ribs, the mapped east pedestrian deck, west curved connecting passage and small station service block. Preserve independent Shibuya Scramble Square, Hikarie, Stream, Fukuras, Sakura Stage, Mark City/Keio host buildings, surrounding property, streets and rail network. Underground Tokyu/metro concourses and the Keio terminal inside its independent Mark City host have no invented separate above-ground building. Current unfinished redevelopment is not replaced by an imagined completed future complex. No trains, people, brands, adverts, lettering, ticket interfaces or navigable railway interiors. Current standard PMTiles retain exact mapped station/terminal footprints and platform polygons. Ordinary 2026 aerial and builder photographs resolve the station frame, surrounding separate towers, concrete entry, white M-section Ginza roof and repeated ribs. Main low station roof11m, Ginza roof19m, east deck13.7m, south hall23.5m and service3.9m follow native height tags; JR platform floor6.2m, raised concourse floor12m and its roof18m, Ginza floor12m and west passage floor6.5m are explicit medium-fi estimates. Hidden JR canopy sections, facade bays, intermediate station levels, live construction inventory and exact platform/road clearances remain approximate. Four illustrative platform stair flights connect the central/south raised halls to the actual platform polygons. Their exact hidden layout is not a surveyed floor plan. Clear roof slots are built around each flight. All station levels are fixed to one common standard field datum 34.911286m at [-65,20]; the unmodified urban field is retained even where roof/vege